# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the Orly TSan CI job (#177).
#
# Format: one rule per line, "<type>:<match>".  E.g. "deadlock:<frame>"
# suppresses a lock-order-inversion (potential deadlock) report whose stack
# contains the named frame; "race:<frame>" suppresses a data race.
#
# Keep this file minimal: every entry must be justified above it as a proven
# false positive, never used to paper over a real race or deadlock.  The
# curated TSan set is GATING (a non-zero warning count fails the job), so a
# real but provably-benign report is documented and suppressed here rather
# than ignored at the job level.
#
# (A prior entry, deadlock:Orly::Spa::FluxCapacitor::TSync::TLocal::IncrLockCount,
# was a test harness lock-order artifact in the SPA flux_capacitor engine; it
# became dead when that engine was deleted in #266 and was removed here.)

# TEMPORARY, a REAL inversion, fixed by #660 (#713).  The orlyi smoke in the
# TSan job reports a cycle between a child repo's DataLock and the Tetris
# player's mutex:
#   - TChild::Refresh, holding the player's mutex, peeks the child's
#     transaction, and the peek opens a TRepo::TView, which takes DataLock;
#   - TRepo::ChangeStatus, holding DataLock, joins the player
#     (TTetrisManager::Join -> TPlayer::OnJoin), which takes the player's mutex.
# Both run on reachable paths, so it is a potential deadlock, not a false
# positive.  #660 (branch ohohoreilly/660-unpause-drain) has Refresh take only
# the holds under the player's mutex and peek after releasing it; with that
# change applied, the smoke reports nothing.  This entry only matches reports
# with Refresh on a stack.  #660 must delete it, and the gate then proves the
# cycle is gone.
deadlock:Orly::Server::TRepoTetrisManager::TPlayer::TChild::Refresh
